Using skills S40 (process implementation), S50 (artifact & I/O), S60 (evaluation/QC), and S30 (plugin extension) to add the baseline classifier and wire it through train/eval.

Implemented a NumPy-based nearest-centroid baseline model with fixed-bin r/theta histograms plus size stats and n_particles features, and hooked it into the wafer_particles model registry and default train config so train/eval emit preds and metrics. The model stores feature spec, scaler, labels, and centroids in `model/model.json` for deterministic eval/predict.

Tests not run (not requested). You can verify with:
